Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for campthehills.net

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this static HTML website following the latest official Vercel documentation.

## What Was Done

### 1. Documentation Research
- Fetched the latest installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Researched the proper implementation method for static HTML sites (without npm/package.json)
- Confirmed the CDN script tag approach is the correct method for HTML-only sites

### 2. Implementation
Added the Vercel Analytics script tag to all HTML pages just before the closing `</head>` tag:

```html
<script defer src="https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js"></script>
```

### 3. Files Modified
- `index.html` - Added Analytics script (line 1855)
- `shows.html` - Added Analytics script (line 1221) 
- `watch.html` - Added Analytics script (line 1604)

## Technical Details

### Why This Approach?
- This is a static HTML website without a build system or package manager
- The CDN script tag method is the official Vercel-recommended approach for HTML5 sites
- The `defer` attribute ensures non-blocking page load for optimal performance

### How It Works
Once deployed to Vercel:
1. The script loads asynchronously from Vercel's CDN
2. Analytics automatically tracks page views and visitor data
3. Data becomes available in the Vercel dashboard under Analytics
4. The `/_vercel/insights/*` routes are automatically configured on deployment

## Next Steps
After this PR is merged and deployed:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (select your project → Analytics → Enable)
2. Wait a few days for traffic data to accumulate
3. View visitor insights in the Vercel Analytics dashboard

## Notes
- No dependencies were added (no package.json needed for static sites)
- No build process required
- Changes are minimal and non-invasive to existing code structure
- The implementation follows official Vercel best practices verified through both documentation and real-world PR examples
